; world-model-pair.fk — the flip/hold probe carried into the world model, and the
; smallest thing that lets a model hold still: a noise floor.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/world-model-update.fk learn/perturbation-pair.fk
;
; WHAT THIS FOUND, before it proposed anything. form-stdlib/world-model-update.fk
; holds the body's update step, and it is unconditional:
;   (defn refine (baseline reading rate) (add baseline (div (sub reading baseline) rate)))
; Every reading moves the baseline. There is nowhere for a reading to be set
; aside. Its band (tests/world-model-update-band.fk, 11111 four-way) carries five
; checks and every one of them is a motion check — surprise is small here, large
; there, novelty moves MORE than familiarity, the shift is 1.25, the novel shift
; exceeds the familiar one. Nothing anywhere asks whether the model can STAY. So
; the world model is, in its shape, the inverter from learn/perturbation-pair.fk:
; it always moves, and a criterion that pays for motion cannot tell it apart from
; one that tracks.
;
; That is not a fault in refine, which does exactly what it says. It is a missing
; probe, and the missing probe hid a missing organ.
;
; THE TWO KINDS, on a world model.
;   FLIP  the world genuinely changed; the model ends CLOSER to the new truth
;   HOLD  the surface changed and the world did not; the model ends where it was
; A flip is read by distance to truth, never by mere difference — one refine step
; at rate 4 covers a quarter of the gap, so "it moved" and "it moved toward what
; is true" are different questions and only the second is asked here.
;
; THE SMALLEST REPAIR: one comparison. Refine only when the surprise clears a
; floor; under it, the baseline is handed back untouched. That is precision-
; weighting in its plainest form — the free energy principle's trust term, written
; as a scalar this body can carry. It is a threshold and it is named as one: the
; body already spends "refuse" on what only a self can do (corpus row 999), and a
; comparison has no ground to borrow that word.
;
; THE GEOMETRY, which is the point. A floor is not set by taste; the pair of
; probes computes the band of floors that lands both. Below the noise the model
; chases every flicker; above the signal it goes deaf. On this body's own
; fixtures — noise surprise 5, signal surprise 100 — the viable band is
; 5 <= floor < 100, and wmp-ok-count measures its width by sweeping. Reasoning
; here is a property of structure, not of size: the entire tunable state of this
; updater is THREE scalars (wmp-state), and the band that makes it correct is
; computed from two probes rather than learned from a corpus.
;
; WHERE THIS CAN GO, named as unfinished work rather than promised.
;   - a floor PER ENTITY. world-model.fk carries people, devices and objects as
;     rows with a kind; a chair's position deserves a higher floor than a person's.
;     The state is already row-shaped, so this wants a column, not an architecture.
;   - a floor LEARNED from witnessed readings instead of set. The sweep here reads
;     eight candidates against two probes; the same loop over a run of real
;     sensings finds the band that held, which is calibration without training.
;   - the floor IS precision in the free energy sense. active-inference.fk counts
;     surprise but does not weight it; wmp-floored is the smallest place that
;     weighting could enter the loop NORTH_STAR.md says does not yet route choices.
;
; Proven by learn/tests/world-model-pair-band.fk, which perturbs its own top
; level: the floor changes the HOLD reading, so bits 2 and 8 cannot both stand
; unless the floor is doing something.
; witnessed: 2026-08-14 -> band 8191 four-way (fkwu / Go / Rust / TS), and
; perturbation-verified live: swap one viable floor in wmp-floors for a deaf one
; and every arm reads 8127 — bit 64 exactly, the width of the measured band.

(do
    ; ---- the fixtures: a baseline, a flicker, a real change ----
    ; FLIP probes carry truth = the world's new value; HOLD probes carry
    ; truth = baseline, because nothing actually changed.
    (defn wmp-base ()   100.0)
    (defn wmp-noise ()  105.0)   ; a surface flicker: surprise 5, world unchanged
    (defn wmp-signal () 200.0)   ; a real change:    surprise 100
    (defn wmp-rate ()   4.0)

    ; ---- did the step land? distance to truth for a flip, stillness for a hold ----
    (defn wmp-closer? (baseline after truth)
        (if (lt (wm-abs (sub after truth)) (wm-abs (sub baseline truth))) 1 0))
    ; stillness is an exact zero shift, not a rounded comparison: the floored step
    ; hands BACK the baseline it was given, so the difference is 0.0 by
    ; construction rather than by luck at some decimal place. This also keeps the
    ; cell inside the minimal walkers' surface — smp reaches math_floor, which the
    ; three walkers do not carry, and a reading no walker can take is not a
    ; four-way reading.
    (defn wmp-stayed? (baseline after)
        (if (eq (wm-abs (sub after baseline)) 0.0) 1 0))

    ; ---- the step as it stands: every reading moves the model ----
    (defn wmp-open (baseline reading) (refine baseline reading (wmp-rate)))

    ; ---- the repair: one comparison. a reading under the floor is set aside. ----
    (defn wmp-floored (baseline reading floor)
        (if (gt (surprise baseline reading) floor)
            (refine baseline reading (wmp-rate))
            baseline))

    ; ---- the two probes, read through each step ----
    (defn wmp-open-flip () (wmp-closer? (wmp-base) (wmp-open (wmp-base) (wmp-signal)) (wmp-signal)))
    (defn wmp-open-hold () (wmp-stayed? (wmp-base) (wmp-open (wmp-base) (wmp-noise))))
    (defn wmp-floored-flip (floor)
        (wmp-closer? (wmp-base) (wmp-floored (wmp-base) (wmp-signal) floor) (wmp-signal)))
    (defn wmp-floored-hold (floor)
        (wmp-stayed? (wmp-base) (wmp-floored (wmp-base) (wmp-noise) floor)))

    ; a floor is viable only when it lands BOTH kinds — the whole-pair reading from
    ; perturbation-pair, carried onto the world model's own operators.
    (defn wmp-floor-ok? (floor)
        (if (eq (wmp-floored-flip floor) 1) (wmp-floored-hold floor) 0))

    ; ---- the sweep: the band is measured, not asserted ----
    (defn wmp-floors () (list 1.0 4.0 5.0 10.0 50.0 99.0 100.0 150.0))
    (defn wmp-ok-count-loop (fs)
        (if (eq (len fs) 0) 0
            (add (wmp-floor-ok? (head fs)) (wmp-ok-count-loop (tail fs)))))
    (defn wmp-ok-count () (wmp-ok-count-loop (wmp-floors)))

    ; ---- the size claim, and the first version of it was a dead check ----
    ; It read (defn wmp-state () (list (wmp-base) (wmp-rate) 5.0)) and the band
    ; asked (eq (len (wmp-state)) 3). That length is 3 BY SYNTAX — a nullary
    ; function over a three-element literal. No input could ever make it fall, so
    ; the bit was benchbench's bb-tag-constant-green wearing a pass, in a band
    ; whose own subject is checks that cannot move. The same shape sits in
    ; grammars/holographic.fk: holo-boundary-size is (len (holo-boundary bulk))
    ; over a four-element list literal and reads 4 even for an EMPTY bulk.
    ;
    ; The living version measures the thing actually claimed: a SHARED floor gives
    ; a state whose length does not grow with the world, and a PER-ENTITY floor
    ; gives one that does. Build both over a small world and a large one; the
    ; shared reading holds while the per-entity reading grows, and if the shared
    ; state ever became per-entity the bit falls.
    (defn wmp-world (n) (if (eq n 0) (empty) (cons n (wmp-world (sub n 1)))))
    (defn wmp-state-shared (w) (list (wmp-base) (wmp-rate) 5.0))
    (defn wmp-floor-each (w)
        (if (eq (len w) 0) (empty) (cons 5.0 (wmp-floor-each (tail w)))))
    (defn wmp-state-per-entity (w)
        (cons (wmp-base) (cons (wmp-rate) (wmp-floor-each w))))

    ; ---- the instrument's own liveness: the floor changes the HOLD reading ----
    (defn wmp-floor-moves? ()
        (if (eq (wmp-open-hold) (wmp-floored-hold 5.0)) 0 1))
    0)
